    "headline": "“So to speak” is a “say” in a hypothetical form: “if one were to say”.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "The Classical Japanese conditional form of the verb 言う (iu, “to say, to speak”): 言わ (iwa, 未然形 (mizenkei, “irrealis form”) of the verb 言う (iu)) + ば (-ba, an inflectional suffix indicating the hypothetical condition)."
      }
    ],
    "examples": [
